WEBVTT

00:30:27.499 --> 00:30:31.105
I'm just curious to hear your reaction
to that set of observations.

00:30:31.591 --> 00:30:34.077
DF: I have described him before as, like,

00:30:34.101 --> 00:30:37.001
the best personal trainer you never had.

00:30:37.025 --> 00:30:42.287
He could get people to push themselves

00:30:42.311 --> 00:30:44.819
to deliver and to achieve

00:30:44.843 --> 00:30:46.866
in ways that they didn't think they could,

00:30:46.890 --> 00:30:48.054
which I think is --

00:30:48.078 --> 00:30:50.602
I think for a lot of us
that's kind of uncomfortable,

00:30:50.626 --> 00:30:51.800
we actually feel bad.

00:30:51.824 --> 00:30:54.690
I think he was able to do it.

00:30:55.086 --> 00:30:57.538
And I think he really believed
he was helping people

00:30:57.562 --> 00:30:59.626
get the most out of their potential.

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:01.680
He was a force, or is a force.